## Problem : Valid Anagram

## Problem Statement : Given two strings s and t, return true if t is an anagram of s, and false otherwise.

 ## Example:
Example 1:

Input: s = "anagram", t = "nagaram"

Output: true

Example 2:

Input: s = "rat", t = "car"

Output: false

## Optimal Approach using Frequency Array 

- take a array of size 256
- first  traverse the loop for str1  and find a character and store in array to convert into ASCII value
- same for str2 and check if freq array value in the given index is less than 0 so returen false otherwise after loop completion return true.
- check, before start looping statement, both str length is same or not. if not, then return return false.

## Code :

class Solution {
    public boolean isAnagram(String s, String t) {

        int[] freq = new int[256];
         if(s.length() != t.length()){
            return false;
         }

        for(int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++){
            freq[s.charAt(i)]+=1; 
        }
        for(int i = 0; i < t.length(); i++){
            freq[t.charAt(i)]-=1; 

            if(freq[t.charAt(i)] < 0) {
                return false;
            }
        }

        return true;
        
    }
}

## Time Complexity :
O(n)
## Space Complexity :
O(1)
